"""Device-side state access for the Android Delta Chat tasks.

Delta Chat keeps its record of conversations in a SQLite database inside the
application's private data directory, and the tasks that produce a file keep it
in the shared storage the file manager and the note editor use.  A judgement
therefore reads two things: the application's own conversation record, and the
files the instruction asked for.

Every read is observational.  The application's database is copied out of the
device and opened read-only, so a judgement cannot modify the account it is
judging.
"""

